#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:1
msgid ""
"To join the WikiToLearn community, you simply have to follow a few easy "
"steps!"
msgstr ""
"¡Pa xunite a la comunidá de WikiToLearn namái tienes de siguir dellos pasos "
"cenciellos!"

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:1
msgid "1 - Create a wiki account"
msgstr "1 - Crea una cuenta wiki"

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:4
msgid ""
"This is very easy, you simply [[Special:CreateAccount|click here]], and you "
"will be able to create your account. Don't forget the e-mail address!"
msgstr ""
"Ye percenciello, namái [[Special:CreateAccount|primi equí]] y sedrás a crear "
"la to cuenta. ¡Nun escaezas la direición de corréu!"

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:4
msgid "2 - Create a chat account"
msgstr "2 - Crea una cuenta de charra"

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:7
msgid ""
"To keep in touch with the community and get help, we use a real time chat "
"system which [https://chat.wikitolearn.org you can find here]. You will be "
"redirected to a channel called [https://chat.wikitolearn.org/channel/general "
"#general]. It is used to speak in general about WikiToLearn. To get help for "
"editing, you can join channels such as [https://chat.wikitolearn.org/channel/"
"help-en #help-en] or [https://chat.wikitolearn.org/channel/help-it #help-"
"it], for help in your preferred language. There also channels that group "
"users coming from the same place. Check out [[Join the WikiToLearn "
"community!/Contributors map|on our map]] to see if there are other "
"contributors near you, and join their channels. If you want to start such a "
"group, just open a new channel (called #h-<city>) and invite to join all "
"users who could be interested. See our guide to the chat on our manual, for "
"further information!"
msgstr ""

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:9
msgid ""
"'''Note that username and password for the chat are unfortunately not the "
"same as for your wiki account! We are working to fix this as soon as we "
"can!'''"
msgstr ""

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:9
msgid "3 - Choose a topic you know about and start editing"
msgstr "3 - Escueyi un tema del que sepas pa entamar a editar"

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:12
msgid ""
"Create a course and start editing! You can either choose to revise existing "
"text, contribute new chapters to existing manuals, or you can create your "
"own thing from scratch."
msgstr ""

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:14
msgid ""
"For the latter, you simply need to go on the department most suited for your "
"material and clicking on the \"Create a course\" link in the blue box!"
msgstr ""

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:16
msgid ""
"Here are more instructions, in case you are a [[<ref:contribute1>|Student]] "
"or a [[<ref:contribute2>|Teacher]]."
msgstr ""
"Equí tán les instrucciones en casu de que seyas un [[<ref:contribute1>|"
"escolín/ina]] o un [[<ref:contribute2>|maestru/a]]."

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:16
msgid "4 - Subscribe to the news channel"
msgstr "4- Soscríbite a la canal d'anuncies"

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:19
msgid ""
"We communicate and updates in several ways. You can check out [https://blogs."
"wikitolearn.org our blogs], or, for more infrequent but meaningful updates, "
"we suggest subscribing [https://telegram.me/WikiToLearnNews to our Telegram "
"news channel]. We also have a [https://www.facebook.com/WikiToLearn Facebook "
"page] and a [https://twitter.com/wikitolearn Twitter account], as well as a "
"[https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC-52KlrKkeA2HcwFzjTGSEw YouTube channel]."
msgstr ""

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:19
msgid "5 - Spread the word!"
msgstr "5 - ¡Espardi'l mensaxe!"

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:22
msgid ""
"WikiToLearn is only possible thanks to a community of enthusiastic users "
"around the world that take on the responsibility of sharing knowledge. But "
"sharing knowledge also means you should share the knowledge that we "
"exist! ;-) A growing community is a great community, and we should all help "
"to make this happen!"
msgstr ""

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:22
msgid "6 - Want to do more?"
msgstr "6 - ¿Quies facer más?"

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:25
msgid ""
"You can be a developer, a translator, an evangelist, and many other things "
"we still haven't thought of! Just get in touch by writing on [https://chat."
"wikitolearn.org/channel/general #general] and somebody will likely be there "
"to guide you. :-)"
msgstr ""

#: guide/en/contribute0.txt:27
msgid ""
"P.S. Did you know we regularly participate in [https://developers.google.com/"
"open-source/gsoc/ Google Summer of Code] and [https://developers.google.com/"
"open-source/gci/ Google Code In]?"
msgstr ""
